# The OKF bundle. NEVER COMMIT THIS.
#
# It is tempting to track bundle/ as "the artifact of record". Do not. A concept
# is not neutral derived data: it carries a document's title, an LLM-written
# summary of its contents, its entities and its full source path. Tracking it
# means every document on your disk gets a searchable description in a hosted
# repository, including the contracts, bank statements and medical letters you
# forgot were in ~/Documents.
#
# Nothing is lost by leaving it untracked. The bundle is rebuildable: `kb bundle`
# writes it from the manifest, and the manifest is rebuildable from the source
# files by `kb scan` and `kb extract`. This ignore rule removes the failure mode
# permanently rather than leaving it as something to keep policing.
#
# If you have already committed a bundle/ and pushed it, rewriting history is not
# enough on a public forge. Treat the contents as disclosed.
bundle/
